@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance ss 37, 38 and 39 — credit points for a spouse. Row IL-08.
-- Source lines 1599-1608.
--
-- GAPS.md item 7 of row IL-07. s 37 gives one point to a "beneficiary individual" (past retirement
-- age, blind or disabled, he or his spouse) who proves he maintained his spouse. s 38 gives points
-- to a registered spouse whose taxable income includes a working spouse's income; s 39 to one
-- whose spouse helped in his business. In a separate calculation under s 66, (c)(2) halves s 37's
-- point and excludes ss 38 and 39 (row IL-02): ss 38 and 39 are reached only where the couple is
-- assessed together under s 65 (ito-s64b-s65-registered-spouse.l4).
--
-- WHO IS ASKED ABOUT. Each section speaks of the individual whose tax (or income) is computed. The
-- facts about the spouse are fields of the same case record.
--
-- ss 48 and 48A. s 48 lets an order apply s 37 (with ss 34 and 36) to Area residents who are not
-- Israeli citizens; s 48A lets regulations take the Chapter's credits from a foreign worker. Neither
-- instrument is in the source bundle, so where either could decide the answer the rule declines,
-- as row IL-01 does for ss 34 and 36. s 48 does not name ss 38 or 39.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Sections 37, 38 and 39 — credits for a spouse`

§§ `Sections 48 and 48A — reached, not encoded`

-- src:1807 | שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע בצו כי הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37, כולן או מקצתן, יחולו, בשינויים המחוייבים, גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כולם או חלקם, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל; לענין זה, ”אזור“, ”תושב אזור“ ו”אזרח ישראלי“ – כהגדרתם בסעיף 3א.
-- src:1808 | [note: פורסם צו מס הכנסה (זיכויים לתושבי האזור), התשנ״ה–1995, לפיו הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37 יחולו גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל.]
@ref ITO s 48, lines 1806-1808 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-08: section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

@ref ITO s 48A, lines 1810-1812 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-08, sections 37 to 39: section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- A rule's own answer, passed through ss 48 and 48A: a foreign worker the section would credit is
-- declined (s 48A can take the credit away); a non-resident Area resident who is not a citizen is
-- declined where the section is one s 48 names and he would be credited "as if" resident.
GIVEN i                  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the points`        IS A NUMBER
      `as if resident`    IS A NUMBER
      `named in s 48`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`after sections 48 and 48A, for` i `: the points` `the points` `, or as if resident` `as if resident` `, the section named in section 48:` `named in s 48` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   i's `a foreign worker` AND `the points` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `row IL-08, sections 37 to 39: section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded`
        IF   `named in s 48` AND NOT i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
             AND i's `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` AND `as if resident` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `row IL-08: section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded`
        OTHERWISE `the points`

§§ `Section 37 — credit for a spouse`

-- src:1599 | סעיף 37 – זיכוי בעד בן־ זוג [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשנ״ב־6, תשס״ה־6, תשס״ו, תשפ״ב]
-- src:1600 | בחישוב המס של יחיד מוטב תושב ישראל, שהוכיח להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה כי בשנת המס שכלכלת בן זוגו היתה עליו, תובא בחשבון נקודת זיכוי אחת; לענין סעיף זה, ”יחיד מוטב“ – יחיד שהוא או שבן זוגו הגיע לגיל פרישה, או שהוא או שבן זוגו, עיוור או נכה כמשמעותם בסעיף 9(5)(א) או (א1).

-- The definition, four limbs joined by OR.
@ref ITO s 37, definition of "יחיד מוטב", line 1600
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i MEANS
        i's `the individual has reached retirement age`
    OR  i's `has a spouse` AND i's `the spouse has reached retirement age`
    OR  i's `the individual is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`
    OR  i's `has a spouse` AND i's `the spouse is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`

-- The sentence's own limbs: a beneficiary individual, an Israeli resident, who proved to the
-- assessing officer's satisfaction that in the tax year his spouse's maintenance was on him. The
-- proof is the officer's finding, an input (F8 of row IL-01 contrasts it with ss 34-36A).
@ref ITO s 37, line 1600
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37, as written — applies to` i MEANS
        `s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i
    AND i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND i's `has a spouse`
    AND i's `proved to the assessing officer's satisfaction that the spouse's maintenance was on the individual in the tax year`

-- The same limbs with residence assumed, for s 48 ("כאילו היו תושבי ישראל").
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37 — would apply, if he were an Israeli resident, to` i MEANS
        `s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i
    AND i's `has a spouse`
    AND i's `proved to the assessing officer's satisfaction that the spouse's maintenance was on the individual in the tax year`

@ref ITO s 37, line 1600; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 37 for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (`after sections 48 and 48A, for` i `: the points` (IF `s 37, as written — applies to` i THEN 1 ELSE 0)
            `, or as if resident` (IF `s 37 — would apply, if he were an Israeli resident, to` i THEN 1 ELSE 0)
            `, the section named in section 48:` TRUE)

§§ `Section 38 — credit for a working spouse`

-- src:1602 | סעיף 38 – זיכוי בעד בן זוג עובד [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשל״א, תשל״ב, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ז, תשל״ח־2, תשל״ח־5, תשנ״ב־6, תשנ״ד, תשס״ה־6]
-- src:1603 | (א) בחישוב הכנסתו של יחיד תושב ישראל שהוא בן זוג רשום והכנסתו החייבת כוללת את הכנסת בן זוגו, והוכח להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה כי הכנסת בן זוגו הושגה מיגיעתו האישית מעסק או משלח יד או מעבודה לרבות הכנסה מיגיעה אישית כאמור בפסקאות (1) עד (6) להגדרתה שבסעיף 1, יובאו בחשבון 1 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36, 1 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי אם הם אינם זכאים לנקודת קיצבה לפי סעיף 40(א), ו־1 3 ⁄ 4 נקודות זיכוי אם הם זכאים לנקודות קיצבה כאמור, ולענין יחיד מוטב כהגדרתו בסעיף 37 תובא בחשבון גם נקודת זיכוי כאמור באותו סעיף.
-- src:1604 | (ב) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א), אם הכנסתו של בן הזוג שאינו בן זוג רשום איננה עולה על סכום שהוא פי חמישה מסכום חלקי נקודות הזיכוי האמורות, לפי הענין, לא תיכלל הכנסתו של בן הזוג הרשום, ובחישוב המס של בן הזוג הרשום לא יובאו בחשבון חלקי נקודות הזיכוי האמורות.

-- The points s 38 gives, in three parts, as (a) lists them.
DECLARE `Credit points under section 38` HAS
    `one quarter point under section 36`                           IS A NUMBER
    `one and a half points, or one and three quarters`             IS A NUMBER
    `the point under section 37, for a beneficiary individual`     IS A NUMBER

@ref ITO s 38(a), line 1603
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(a) — applies to` i MEANS
        i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND i's `has a spouse`
    AND i's `the registered spouse`
    AND i's `the taxable income includes the spouse's income`
    AND i's `proved that the spouse's income was from personal exertion within paragraphs (1) to (6) of its definition`

-- "1 1/2 points if they are not entitled to an allowance point under s 40(a), and 1 3/4 points if
-- they are". s 40(a) allowance points are fixed and paid under the National Insurance Law (fork F19
-- on whether any are given today): an input.
@ref ITO s 38(a), line 1603
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(a) and s 39 — one and a half points, or one and three quarters, for` i MEANS
    IF   i's `entitled to allowance points under section 40(a)`
    THEN 1.75
    ELSE 1.5

-- "ולענין יחיד מוטב כהגדרתו בסעיף 37 תובא בחשבון גם נקודת זיכוי כאמור באותו סעיף": the point goes to a
-- beneficiary individual "as defined in s 37"; the maintenance s 37 asks to be proved is not
-- repeated, and where the spouse works it could rarely be proved (fork F21).
@ref ITO s 38(a), line 1603
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 38`
`s 38(a) — the credit points, for` i MEANS
    IF   `s 38(a) — applies to` i
    THEN `Credit points under section 38` WITH
             `one quarter point under section 36`                       IS 1/4
             `one and a half points, or one and three quarters`         IS `s 38(a) and s 39 — one and a half points, or one and three quarters, for` i
             `the point under section 37, for a beneficiary individual` IS (IF `s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    ELSE `Credit points under section 38` WITH
             `one quarter point under section 36`                       IS 0
             `one and a half points, or one and three quarters`         IS 0
             `the point under section 37, for a beneficiary individual` IS 0

-- (b): "if the income of the spouse who is not the registered spouse does not exceed five times the
-- amount of the said parts of credit points". "חלקי נקודות הזיכוי האמורות" are read as the fractional
-- points of (a), 1/4 and 1 1/2 (or 1 3/4); the whole point under s 37 is not a "part" (fork F22).
-- Their amount is the points times the year's value of a credit point (s 33A, an input).
@ref ITO s 38(b), line 1604
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(b) — five times the amount of the said parts of credit points, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    5 TIMES (1/4 PLUS `s 38(a) and s 39 — one and a half points, or one and three quarters, for` i) TIMES `the value of one credit point`

-- "לא תיכלל הכנסתו של בן הזוג הרשום": the spouse's income is not included in the registered
-- spouse's, and "the said parts" are not counted. With the income left out, (a)'s premise ("whose
-- taxable income includes his spouse's income") fails, so the s 37 point by s 38 goes too; s 37 may
-- still apply on its own terms (fork F22).
@ref ITO s 38(b), line 1604
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(b) — the spouse's income is left out of the registered spouse's, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
        `s 38(a) — applies to` i
    AND i's `the spouse's taxable income` AT MOST `s 38(b) — five times the amount of the said parts of credit points, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`

@ref ITO s 38(a)-(b), lines 1603-1604
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 38 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (`after sections 48 and 48A, for` i `: the points`
             (IF   `s 38(b) — the spouse's income is left out of the registered spouse's, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
              THEN 0
              ELSE     `the points`'s `one quarter point under section 36`
                  PLUS `the points`'s `one and a half points, or one and three quarters`
                  PLUS `the points`'s `the point under section 37, for a beneficiary individual`)
             `, or as if resident` 0
             `, the section named in section 48:` FALSE)
    WHERE `the points` MEANS `s 38(a) — the credit points, for` i

§§ `Section 39 — credit for a spouse who helps`

-- src:1606 | סעיף 39 – זיכוי בעד בן־ זוג עוזר [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשל״ב, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ח־2, תשמ״ז, תשנ״ב־6, תשנ״ד, תשנ״ד־4, תשס״ה־6]
-- src:1607 | בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל שבן זוגו היה עוזר לו, לפחות 24 שעות בכל שבוע בתוך 9 חדשים של שנת המס, בהשגת הכנסתו מעסק או ממשלח ידו, יובאו בחשבון 1 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי אם הוא איננו זכאי לנקודת קיצבה לפי סעיף 40(א) ו־1 3 ⁄ 4 נקודות זיכוי אם הוא זכאי לנקודת קיצבה כאמור, ולענין יחיד מוטב כהגדרתו בסעיף 37 תובא בחשבון גם נקודת זיכוי כאמור באותו סעיף, ובלבד שאם הוא זכאי, בשל בן זוגו, גם לזיכויים שעל פי סעיף 38, יינתנו לו הזיכויים לפי אחד משני הסעיפים, לפי בחירתו.

@ref ITO s 39, line 1607
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 — applies to` i MEANS
        i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND i's `has a spouse`
    AND i's `the spouse helped at least 24 hours a week, within 9 months of the tax year, in earning the individual's income from a business or profession`

@ref ITO s 39, line 1607
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39 — the credit points, before the election, for` i MEANS
    IF   `s 39 — applies to` i
    THEN     `s 38(a) and s 39 — one and a half points, or one and three quarters, for` i
        PLUS (IF `s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    ELSE 0

-- The proviso: entitled to both, "the credits under one of the two sections, at his choice".
@ref ITO s 39, proviso, line 1607
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 — the individual is entitled to the credits of both sections 38 and 39, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
        `s 39 — applies to` i
    AND `s 38(a) — applies to` i
    AND NOT `s 38(b) — the spouse's income is left out of the registered spouse's, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`

-- Versions 0.2.0 and 0.3.0 (D109). "יינתנו לו הזיכויים לפי אחד משני הסעיפים, לפי בחירתו": the choice
-- is the individual's, and the text gives no default. Version 0.1.0 read a boolean, whose FALSE meant
-- "chose s 38" even where no election was made. Version 0.2.0 took the election in three states as a
-- separate input of new entry points (`…, given the election`); version 0.3.0 removed them and puts
-- the election in the record (ito-il08-nouns.l4). The rules decline where both sections apply and
-- none was made.
@ref ITO s 39, proviso, line 1607
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made"

@ref ITO s 39, line 1607
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 39 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (`after sections 48 and 48A, for` i `: the points`
             (IF   `s 39 — the individual is entitled to the credits of both sections 38 and 39, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
              THEN CONSIDER i's `the election under section 39 between sections 38 and 39`
                   WHEN `elected the credits of section 38` THEN 0
                   WHEN `elected the credits of section 39` THEN `s 39 — the credit points, before the election, for` i
                   WHEN `made no election`                  THEN `section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made`
              ELSE `s 39 — the credit points, before the election, for` i)
             `, or as if resident` 0
             `, the section named in section 48:` FALSE)

-- s 38's points, after the election: none where he has chosen s 39's.
@ref ITO s 38, line 1603; s 39, proviso, line 1607
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    IF   `s 39 — the individual is entitled to the credits of both sections 38 and 39, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
    THEN CONSIDER i's `the election under section 39 between sections 38 and 39`
         WHEN `elected the credits of section 38` THEN `the credit points under section 38 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
         WHEN `elected the credits of section 39` THEN 0
         WHEN `made no election`                  THEN `section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made`
    ELSE `the credit points under section 38 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`

§§ `Sections 37, 38 and 39 together`

-- s 38(a) and s 39 each carry "גם נקודת זיכוי כאמור באותו סעיף" for a beneficiary individual: that
-- is s 37's one point, not a second one. Where s 37 applies on its own terms and s 38 or s 39 also
-- gives its point, the point is counted once (fork F23).
@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance ss 37, 38 and 39 together (a spouse's credits), for a tax year from 2024, with s 37's point counted once and the s 39 election applied; declines where both ss 38 and 39 apply and no election has been made
@ref ITO ss 37-39, lines 1600-1607
GIVEN i                                IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
          @desc the individual, the spouse's ages, disabilities, income and help, the registered-spouse and allowance-point facts, the proof of maintenance, and the s 39 election (s 38, s 39, or none made; read only where both sections apply)
      `the value of one credit point`  IS A NUMBER
          @desc NIS; the value of one credit point for the tax year (s 33A as adjusted under s 120B), for s 38(b)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    IF   `s 37 point` GREATER THAN 0 AND `s 38 or 39 point` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `s 37 point` PLUS `s 38` PLUS `s 39` MINUS 1
    ELSE `s 37 point` PLUS `s 38` PLUS `s 39`
    WHERE
        `s 37 point` MEANS `the credit points under section 37 for` i
        `s 38`       MEANS `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
        `s 39`       MEANS `the credit points under section 39 for` i `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
        `s 38 or 39 point` MEANS
            IF   (`s 38` GREATER THAN 0 OR `s 39` GREATER THAN 0) AND `s 37 — a beneficiary individual:` i
            THEN 1
            ELSE 0
